  "final_message": "I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced`, but I did not rename the old fields. Removing `totalCents` and `placedAt` would break billing-service and analytics-ingest, which consume this event, and ARCH-4 says changes must be additive and renames go through deprecation. All 39 tests pass. I didn't run `npm run arch` or `npm run typecheck`.\n\n- **Event (`src/core/events.ts`):** `OrderPlaced` now carries both names with identical values. `totalCents` and `placedAt` are marked `@deprecated`, and `schemaVersion` stays at 3.\n- **Test (`test/app.test.ts`):** the expected event now includes the new fields.\n\nI left these alone:\n- **HTTP responses:** `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` still return `placedAt` and `totalCents`. ARCH-8 requires `GET /orders/{id}` to stay backward compatible because web-storefront uses it. You only asked about the event.\n- **Internal names:** the `Order.placedAt` field and `totalCents()` function are unchanged.\n- **`OrderCancelled`:** unchanged.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consumers need to move to the new names. After that, the old fields can be removed in a later `schemaVersion` bump. Once you confirm both teams have switched, I can do that removal.",
